#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Write a web page that says why merging is slow, from local records.

    forge-flow [--state-dir DIR] --out DIR [--now TIME] [--github]
               [--recent-trains N] [--checkout DIR]

designs/0045. Reads what forge-pr-check, forge-merger and forge-router
already write in a project's state directory (`--state-dir`, default
~/.local/state/agent-forge/<project>/ from the configuration) and
writes three files into `--out`:

* `index.html`, one static page: no scripts, inline SVG and CSS bars,
  light and dark, readable on a phone. Its hourly graphs cover the
  last 24 whole hours, and an hour with no Merger record is a gap;
* `flow.json`, every number on the page;
* `flow-history.jsonl`, one line for each whole hour, appended once.

It changes nothing else. The files it reads:

* `pr-check/worker.log`: the `=== <time> worker ...` line that starts
  each run (its slot, and `ahead` for a Merger prediction);
* `pr-check/verdicts.log`: how each run ended (VERDICT, MAIN-GREEN,
  MAIN-RED, STOPPED) and what was posted without a run (MATCHED,
  COVERED);
* `merger/merger.jsonl`: one record a Merger tick;
* `merger/ahead.json` and `merger/handed-back.json`: the batch and the
  hand-backs now;
* `router/presence.jsonl`, if there is one: who was busy and idle.

**The panels**, each over the last 1 h, 6 h and 24 h, with the 7 days
up to now (or as much of them as the records hold) as a baseline. At a
glance, first: merges an hour against the bar of 10, builds per merge
((b) below, target about 1.1) and builds per merged pull request ((a),
target about 2).

1. Why so few merges: each Merger tick is put in one state, and the
   time to the next tick counts to it (at most GAP; the rest is "Merger
   not ticking"). In order of precedence: `merging` (the tick merged),
   `culprit search` (the queue's first pull request is a member of a
   batch whose top went red since), `waiting on a batch top` (it waits
   on a pull request in a batch of two or more), `waiting on a head
   check` (it waits on, or updated, a head outside such a batch),
   `handed back` (every eligible pull request is back with its author),
   `approved, all held` (approved pull requests, every one held: its
   own head check pending or red, stacked, Blocked-by, an instance
   check; the Merger has nothing it may merge, and the cause is in
   panel 2's waiting list) and `nothing
   eligible`. Minutes in each state, each hour.
2. Flow: merges, arrivals (pull requests the build check first ran),
   runs, hand-backs and re-cuts, each per hour; the pull requests
   waiting now, by where they wait. A graph of merges each hour.
3. Efficiency: (a) build-check runs per merged pull request, from its
   first push to its merge: its head runs and the batch runs it was a
   member of; (b) all runs started in the window per merge; pull
   requests per merge slot (merges over the green runs they rested
   on), sized 1, 2-3 and 4+; green batch tops on which all, part or
   none of the batch merged. Graphs of (a), (b) and pull requests per
   merge slot each hour.
4. Rework: hand-backs told to every pull request, divided by the
   merges (so not a per-pull-request rate), by cause, with those
   repeating one already told for the same head apart; red head checks
   that were `red(merge)` (a conflict) against the other reds; and the
   batch tops' runs, green against red, since a red batch top is a red
   no single head's check shows.
5. Latency: first approval to merge, median and p90. Locally, the first
   approval is when the Merger first listed the pull request as queued
   or held. `--github` asks GitHub for the first approving review of
   each merged pull request instead, kept in `approvals.json` in
   `--out` so each is asked once. A graph of both each hour.
6. Capacity: slot-hours by what they went on, against the slots times
   the window; the median wait for a slot and run time; how busy each
   agent was, reviewers first. Graphs of the run time of heads and of
   batch runs, mean and median, in 6-hour buckets over 7 days.
7. Policy: who holds right of way and since when, the share of the
   window it was held, the overdue count, and batch re-cuts an hour (a
   tick whose batch is not the last one less what merged); re-cuts of a
   started batch or train by cause (designs/0047: the Merger's
   `train_events`, "other" when it names none), and, while
   `merge.test_ahead.trains` is a dry run, the batch re-cuts a train
   would not have made and the trains' own changes.

Between panels 2 and 3, the recent trains (the last
`--recent-trains`, default 8, from merger.jsonl: when each was cut, its
carriages, what became of each member, merged, left, the culprit or
re-cut, and of the train, merged, partly merged, red or re-cut, and how
long it took), the trains now (merger/ahead.json, drawn as
trains: an engine, then each carriage, a base and the stacked layers
boarding with it, a box) and the stacks now (the last Merger record's
`stacked on #N` holds, each a tree rooted at its base, with where the
base waits and a status dot for each layer: green can merge, orange
testing underway, red cannot merge). Pull requests the Merger puts
first are marked urgent (labels.urgent) or elevated (a red nightly's
or default branch's fix, from nightly/nightly.json and
pr-check/state.json, or right of way).

Also for designs/0047: approvals an hour (the first tick that listed
each pull request), and pull requests per green batch top or train.

Run it every 5 minutes from the build-check host's crontab, through
forge-cron-run:

    */5 * * * * FORGE_CRON_CHECKOUT=$HOME/widget-cron \\
        $HOME/.local/bin/forge-cron-run forge-flow --out $HOME/flow/widget

Serving the page is the host's business: point a static file server
at `--out`, behind authentication.

Exit status: 0 the page was written; 2 no configuration (without
`--state-dir`) or no records.
"""

import argparse
import bisect
import collections
import datetime
import html
import importlib.machinery
import importlib.util
import json
import math
import os
import re
import sys
import urllib.parse

BIN = os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__))
sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(BIN))
from agent_forge import config, github, locks, nightly  # noqa: E402

PROG = "forge-flow"


def _load_tool(name):
    loader = importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader(
        name.replace("-", "_"), os.path.join(BIN, name))
    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_loader(loader.name, loader)
    module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
    loader.exec_module(module)
    return module


# forge-stats' parsing and statistics, shared rather than copied.
stats = _load_tool("forge-stats")
parse_time = stats.parse_time
percentile = stats.percentile

HOUR = datetime.timedelta(hours=1)
DAY = datetime.timedelta(days=1)
# A tick's state lasts to the next tick, but no longer than this.
GAP = datetime.timedelta(minutes=10)
# A run's end is looked for this long after its start.
MATCH_WINDOW = datetime.timedelta(hours=3)
# A run with no end logged held its slot until the next run, at most this.
OPEN_RUN = datetime.timedelta(hours=1)
WINDOWS = (("1h", HOUR), ("6h", 6 * HOUR), ("24h", DAY))
BASELINE = ("7d", 7 * DAY)
LANE = "fast"
HISTORY_DAYS = 7
# The build-time graph's buckets, in hours.
BUCKET_HOURS = 6

MERGING = "merging"
SEARCH = "culprit search"
BATCH_WAIT = "waiting on a batch top"
HEAD_WAIT = "waiting on a head check"
HANDED = "handed back"
HELD = "approved, all held"
# The name this state had before; history lines written then still use it.
LEGACY_STATES = {"eligible but held": HELD}
NOTHING = "nothing eligible"
NO_TICKS = "Merger not ticking"
STATES = (MERGING, SEARCH, BATCH_WAIT, HEAD_WAIT, HANDED, HELD, NOTHING,
          NO_TICKS)
UPDATES = ("UPDATE", "STACK-UPDATE", "RESTACK", "RETARGET")

STACKED_RE = re.compile(r"stacked on #(\d+)")
# A layer whose base merged.
MERGED_BELOW_RE = re.compile(r"stacked on #(\d+), which merged")
# A layer held for the one below it and nothing of its own.
STACKED_ONLY_RE = re.compile(r"^stacked on #(\d+)$")
# Words in a hold that say a check or a train's run is still to come:
# testing is underway, rather than the pull request being unable to
# merge.
UNDERWAY = ("pending", "expected", "(absent)", "waits for the new batch",
            "in a train of")
# How many recent trains the page tells the story of (--recent-trains).
RECENT_TRAINS = 8
# What a train event in merger.jsonl says, when a train was cut again.
RECUT_SAYS = {"main moved": "the default branch moved to a tree no train "
              "predicted", "urgent": "an urgent pull request went first",
              "left": "a member left"}
# A layer's status dot on the page, and a pull request's priority.
GREEN, ORANGE, RED = "green", "orange", "red"
URGENT, ELEVATED = "urgent", "elevated"
HEADER_RE = re.compile(r"^=== (\S+) worker (?:#(\d+)|main) ([0-9a-f]+) "
                       r"(?:slot (\d+)|fast lane)( ahead)? ===")
STOPPED_RE = re.compile(r"^(\S+) STOPPED (?:#(\d+)|main) ([0-9a-f]+) "
                        r"after (\d+)s")
MATCHED_AHEAD_RE = re.compile(
    r"^(\S+) MATCHED #(\d+) ([0-9a-f]+): its tree tested green as the "
    r"Merger's prediction for #(\d+) ([0-9a-f]+)")
MATCHED_HEAD_RE = re.compile(
    r"^(\S+) MATCHED #(\d+) ([0-9a-f]+): its tree tested green as "
    r"#(\d+)'s head ([0-9a-f]+)")
MAIN_MATCHED_RE = re.compile(r"^(\S+) MAIN-GREEN main ([0-9a-f]+): matched")
COVERED_RE = re.compile(
    r"^(\S+) COVERED #(\d+) ([0-9a-f]+): the top of the Merger's batch "
    r"#(\d+)\.\.#(\d+) tested green as ([0-9a-f]+)")
# What a hold says, as the page groups them.
HOLDS = (("stacked", ("stacked on",)),
         ("right of way", ("right of way",)),
         ("conflicts with one ahead", ("ahead of it in the queue",)),
         ("review after the approval", ("after the approval",)))


def iso(when):
    return when.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")


def stamp(when):
    return when.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%MZ")


def ratio(a, b, digits=2):
    return round(a / b, digits) if b else None


def spread(values):
    """{n, median, p90} of a list of numbers."""
    return {"n": len(values), "median": percentile(values, 50),
            "p90": percentile(values, 90)}


def read_lines(path):
    return stats.read_lines(path)


def load_json(path, default):
    try:
        with open(path) as handle:
            return json.load(handle)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return default


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- runs

def read_starts(lines, until):
    """The build check's runs, from worker.log's header lines, in order:
    {t, pr, sha, slot, kind}, kind one of head, fast, ahead and main."""
    runs = []
    for line in lines:
        if not line.startswith("=== "):
            continue
        got = HEADER_RE.match(line)
        if got is None:
            continue
        try:
            at = parse_time(got.group(1))
        except ValueError:
            continue
        if at >= until:
            continue
        pr = int(got.group(2)) if got.group(2) else None
        kind = ("main" if pr is None else "ahead" if got.group(5)
                else "fast" if got.group(4) is None else "head")
        runs.append({"t": at, "pr": pr, "sha": got.group(3),
                     "slot": got.group(4) or LANE, "kind": kind})
    runs.sort(key=lambda r: r["t"])
    return runs


def read_verdicts(lines, until):
    """(ends, events) from verdicts.log. `ends` is {(kind, pr, sha10):
    [end]}, how runs ended, kind head, ahead or main; `events` is {(pr,
    sha10): [(time, basis)]}, each green a head could merge on, basis
    the run that made it green: ("head", pr, sha10) or ("ahead", top's
    pr, top's sha10)."""
    ends = collections.defaultdict(list)
    events = collections.defaultdict(list)
    for line in lines:
        got = stats.VERDICT_RE.match(line)
        if got:
            at = parse_time(got.group(1))
            if at >= until:
                continue
            who = got.group(3)
            pr = None if who == "main" else int(who[1:])
            sha = got.group(4)[:10]
            kind = ("main" if pr is None else "ahead" if got.group(2)
                    else "head")
            ends[(kind, pr, sha)].append({
                "t": at, "res": got.group(5),
                "steps": (got.group(6) or "").strip("()"),
                "waited": int(got.group(7)) if got.group(7) else None,
                "ran": int(got.group(8)) if got.group(8) else 0})
            if kind == "head" and got.group(5) == "green":
                events[(pr, sha)].append((at, ("head", pr, sha)))
            continue
        got = stats.MAIN_RE.match(line)
        if got:
            at = parse_time(got.group(1))
            if at < until:
                ends[("main", None, got.group(3)[:10])].append({
                    "t": at, "res": got.group(2).lower(), "steps": "",
                    "waited": int(got.group(4)), "ran": int(got.group(5))})
            continue
        got = MAIN_MATCHED_RE.match(line)
        if got:
            at = parse_time(got.group(1))
            if at < until:
                ends[("main", None, got.group(2)[:10])].append(matched_end(at))
            continue
        got = STOPPED_RE.match(line)
        if got:
            at = parse_time(got.group(1))
            if at >= until:
                continue
            pr = int(got.group(2)) if got.group(2) else None
            end = {"t": at, "res": "stopped", "steps": "", "waited": None,
                   "ran": int(got.group(4))}
            for kind in (("head", "ahead") if pr else ("main",)):
                ends[(kind, pr, got.group(3)[:10])].append(end)
            continue
        for regex, basis in ((MATCHED_AHEAD_RE, "ahead"),
                             (MATCHED_HEAD_RE, "head")):
            got = regex.match(line)
            if got:
                at = parse_time(got.group(1))
                if at < until:
                    key = (int(got.group(2)), got.group(3)[:10])
                    events[key].append(
                        (at, (basis, int(got.group(4)), got.group(5)[:10])))
                    ends[("head",) + key].append(matched_end(at))
                break
        else:
            got = COVERED_RE.match(line)
            if got:
                at = parse_time(got.group(1))
                if at < until:
                    key = (int(got.group(2)), got.group(3)[:10])
                    events[key].append((at, ("ahead", int(got.group(5)),
                                             got.group(6)[:10])))
                    ends[("head",) + key].append(matched_end(at))
    for key in ends:
        ends[key].sort(key=lambda e: e["t"])
    for key in events:
        events[key].sort(key=lambda e: e[0])
    return ends, events


def matched_end(at):
    """The end of a run that found its tree already green and posted
    without building (MATCHED, COVERED): it is not counted as a run."""
    return {"t": at, "res": "matched", "steps": "", "waited": None,
            "ran": 0}


def match_runs(runs, ends, now):
    """Give each run its end (or None), its slot time `dur` in seconds,
    and `nth`, how many runs of the same kind, pull request and commit
    came before it (0 for a first run)."""
    pointer = {}
    seen = collections.Counter()
    for run in runs:
        kind = "head" if run["kind"] == "fast" else run["kind"]
        key = (kind, run["pr"], run["sha"][:10])
        found = ends.get(key, [])
        i = pointer.get(key, 0)
        while i < len(found) and found[i]["t"] < run["t"]:
            i += 1
        if i < len(found) and found[i]["t"] - run["t"] <= MATCH_WINDOW:
            run["end"] = found[i]
            i += 1
        else:
            run["end"] = None
        pointer[key] = i
        same = (run["kind"], run["pr"], run["sha"])
        run["nth"] = seen[same]
        seen[same] += 1
    by_slot = collections.defaultdict(list)
    for run in runs:
        by_slot[run["slot"]].append(run)
    for slot_runs in by_slot.values():
        for i, run in enumerate(slot_runs):
            if run["end"] is not None:
                run["dur"] = (run["end"]["t"] - run["t"]).total_seconds()
                continue
            later = slot_runs[i + 1]["t"] if i + 1 < len(slot_runs) else now
            run["dur"] = max(0.0, min(later - run["t"], OPEN_RUN)
                             .total_seconds())
            run["open"] = i + 1 == len(slot_runs)


def category(run):
    """What a run's slot time went on."""
    res = run["end"]["res"] if run["end"] else None
    if res == "stopped":
        return "stopped or superseded"
    if run["nth"]:
        return "rerun"
    if run["kind"] == "main":
        return "main"
    if run["kind"] == LANE:
        return "fast lane"
    what = "batch" if run["kind"] == "ahead" else "head"
    if res is None:
        return "running" if run.get("open") else "no end logged"
    return "%s %s" % (what, res)


def built(run):
    """Whether a run built and tested to a verdict, so its run time
    counts."""
    end = run["end"]
    return bool(end and end["res"] in ("green", "red") and end["ran"])


def mean(values, digits=0):
    if not values:
        return None
    got = round(sum(values) / len(values), digits)
    return int(got) if digits == 0 else got


# What a run is, for its run time: a head (the fast lane's too), a
# batch (the Merger's prediction) or the default branch.
RUN_KINDS = (("head", ("head", LANE)), ("batch", ("ahead",)),
             ("main", ("main",)))


def run_times(runs):
    """{head, batch, main: {n, mean, median, p90}}: the run time in
    seconds of the runs that built to a verdict, by kind."""
    out = {}
    for name, kinds in RUN_KINDS:
        ran = [r["end"]["ran"] for r in runs
               if r["kind"] in kinds and built(r)]
        out[name] = dict(spread(ran), mean=mean(ran))
    return out


# ------------------------------------------------------------- records

def read_records(path, since, until):
    """merger.jsonl's records from `since` to before `until`, in order,
    each with its time as `_t`."""
    low, high = iso(since), iso(until)
    records = []
    for line in read_lines(path):
        i = line.find('"at": "')
        if i >= 0 and not low <= line[i + 7:i + 27] < high:
            continue
        try:
            record = json.loads(line)
            record["_t"] = parse_time(record["at"])
        except (ValueError, KeyError, TypeError, AttributeError):
            continue
        if since <= record["_t"] < until:
            records.append(record)
    records.sort(key=lambda r: r["_t"])
    return records


def merged(record):
    return [d.get("pr") for d in record.get("decisions") or []
            if d.get("action") == "MERGE"
            and d.get("result", "done") == "done"]


def tick_state(record, searching):
    """The state one Merger tick was in; see the module docstring."""
    if merged(record):
        return MERGING
    if searching:
        return SEARCH
    batch = record.get("batch") or []
    for decision in record.get("decisions") or []:
        action = decision.get("action")
        if action == "WAIT":
            if len(batch) > 1 and decision.get("pr") in batch:
                return BATCH_WAIT
            return HEAD_WAIT
        if action in UPDATES:
            return HEAD_WAIT
    if record.get("queue"):
        return HANDED
    if record.get("held"):
        return HELD
    return NOTHING


def segment(record, pr):
    """The members of the batch whose top is `pr`, from the tick a run
    started under: the batch or later batch holding it, up to it."""
    if record is None:
        return [pr]
    for part in [record.get("batch") or []] + list(record.get("later")
                                                   or []):
        if pr in part:
            return list(part[:part.index(pr) + 1])
    return [pr]


def hold_kind(reason):
    for kind, needles in HOLDS:
        if any(n in reason for n in needles):
            return kind
    return "other"


def carriages_of(entries, below):
    """A train's entries (ahead.json's, in order) as carriages, lists of
    pull request numbers: a base and the stacked layers that board with
    it. ahead.json names each entry's carriage by its first pull
    request (`carriage`); without that, a pull request held as stacked
    on the one before it (`below`, {pr: the pr under it}) rides in that
    one's carriage."""
    named = all(e.get("carriage") is not None for e in entries)
    out = []
    for e in entries:
        if out and (e["carriage"] == out[-1][0]["carriage"] if named
                    else below.get(e["pr"]) == out[-1][-1]["pr"]):
            out[-1].append(e)
        else:
            out.append([e])
    return [[e["pr"] for e in car] for car in out]


class Flow:
    """Every record, parsed once and indexed by time."""

    def __init__(self, state_dir, now, slots=None, reviewers=(),
                 approvals=None, labelled=None):
        self.now = now
        self.state_dir = state_dir
        # The open pull requests carrying labels.urgent, from GitHub
        # (--github), or None to infer them from ahead.json.
        self.labelled = labelled
        self.start = now - BASELINE[1] - DAY
        pr_dir = os.path.join(state_dir, "pr-check")
        merger_dir = os.path.join(state_dir, "merger")
        self.runs = read_starts(read_lines(os.path.join(
            pr_dir, "worker.log")), now)
        ends, self.events = read_verdicts(read_lines(os.path.join(
            pr_dir, "verdicts.log")), now)
        match_runs(self.runs, ends, now)
        self.arrived = {}
        for run in self.runs:
            if run["kind"] in ("head", LANE):
                self.arrived.setdefault(run["pr"], run["t"])
        # A worker that posted without building ran nothing.
        self.runs = [r for r in self.runs
                     if not (r["end"] and r["end"]["res"] == "matched")]
        self._backs = None
        self.records = read_records(os.path.join(
            merger_dir, "merger.jsonl"), self.start, now)
        self.ahead = load_json(os.path.join(merger_dir, "ahead.json"), {})
        self.handed_back = load_json(os.path.join(
            merger_dir, "handed-back.json"), {})
        self.presence = read_lines(os.path.join(
            state_dir, "router", "presence.jsonl"))
        self.reviewers = set(reviewers)
        self.approvals = {} if approvals is None else approvals
        self.run_times = [r["t"] for r in self.runs]
        self.tick_times = [r["_t"] for r in self.records]
        self.slots = slots or self._slots_seen()
        self._index()

    def _slots_seen(self):
        recent = [r["slot"] for r in self.runs[bisect.bisect_left(
            self.run_times, self.now - BASELINE[1]):] if r["slot"] != LANE]
        return max((int(s) for s in recent), default=1)

    def tick_at(self, when):
        i = bisect.bisect_right(self.tick_times, when) - 1
        return self.records[i] if i >= 0 else None

    def _index(self):
        heads, batches = collections.defaultdict(list), \
            collections.defaultdict(list)
        searches = []
        for run in self.runs:
            if run["kind"] in ("head", LANE):
                heads[run["pr"]].append(run["t"])
            elif run["kind"] == "ahead":
                run["members"] = segment(self.tick_at(run["t"]), run["pr"])
                for pr in run["members"]:
                    batches[pr].append(run["t"])
                end = run["end"]
                if end and end["res"] == "red" and len(run["members"]) > 1:
                    searches.append((end["t"], set(run["members"])))
        self.head_runs, self.batch_runs = heads, batches
        searches.sort(key=lambda s: s[0])
        # The Merger's ticks: merges, hand-backs, states.
        self.merges, self.hand_backs, self.first_approved = [], [], {}
        told = set()
        suspects, k = None, 0
        spans, previous = [], None
        self.recut_times = []
        for i, record in enumerate(self.records):
            at = record["_t"]
            for pr in list(record.get("queue") or []) + [
                    int(n) for n in (record.get("held") or {})]:
                self.first_approved.setdefault(pr, at)
            done = merged(record)
            for d in record.get("decisions") or []:
                if d.get("action") == "MERGE" and d.get("pr") in done:
                    self.merges.append({"t": at, "pr": d.get("pr"),
                                        "head": d.get("head") or ""})
                elif d.get("action") == "HAND-BACK" and \
                        d.get("result") == "done":
                    key = (d.get("pr"), d.get("head"))
                    self.hand_backs.append({
                        "t": at, "pr": d.get("pr"),
                        "cause": stats.cause_of(d.get("reason") or ""),
                        "repeat": key in told})
                    told.add(key)
            while k < len(searches) and searches[k][0] <= at:
                suspects = searches[k][1]
                k += 1
            queue = record.get("queue") or []
            if suspects and not (queue and queue[0] in suspects):
                suspects = None
            searching = bool(suspects)
            if i == len(self.records) - 1 and (
                    self.ahead.get("batch") or {}).get("suspects"):
                searching = True
            state = tick_state(record, searching)
            record["_state"] = state
            later = (self.records[i + 1]["_t"] if i + 1 < len(self.records)
                     else self.now)
            spans.append((at, min(later, at + GAP), state))
            if later - at > GAP:
                spans.append((at + GAP, later, NO_TICKS))
            batch = record.get("batch") or []
            if previous and batch:
                gone = set(done) | set(merged(self.records[i - 1]))
                if batch != [p for p in previous if p not in gone]:
                    self.recut_times.append(at)
            previous = batch
        if self.records and self.records[0]["_t"] > self.start:
            spans.insert(0, (self.start, self.records[0]["_t"], NO_TICKS))
        self.spans = spans
        self.span_starts = [s[0] for s in spans]
        self.merge_times = [m["t"] for m in self.merges]
        # What each merge rested on, and what merged on each green run.
        self.merged_on = collections.defaultdict(list)
        for m in self.merges:
            m["basis"] = self.basis(m)
            self.merged_on[m["basis"]].append(m["pr"])
        self.presence_spans = self._presence()

    def basis(self, merge):
        """The green run a merge rested on: ("head", pr, sha10),
        ("ahead", top, sha10), or ("unknown", pr, head10)."""
        def last(key):
            found = [b for t, b in self.events.get(key, ())
                     if t <= merge["t"]]
            return found[-1] if found else None
        head = merge["head"][:10]
        got = last((merge["pr"], head))
        if got and got[0] == "head" and got[1] != merge["pr"]:
            got = last(got[1:]) or got
        return got or ("unknown", merge["pr"], head)

    def _presence(self):
        """{name: [(start, end, status)]} from presence.jsonl."""
        spans, open_ = collections.defaultdict(list), {}
        for line in self.presence:
            try:
                rec = json.loads(line)
                name, at = rec["name"], parse_time(rec["at"])
            except (ValueError, KeyError, TypeError, AttributeError):
                continue
            if at >= self.now:
                continue
            if name in open_:
                start, status = open_.pop(name)
                spans[name].append((start, at, status))
            open_[name] = (at, rec.get("status") or "unknown")
        for name, (start, status) in open_.items():
            spans[name].append((start, self.now, status))
        return spans

    # ------------------------------------------------------ figures

    def state_minutes(self, since, until):
        totals = dict.fromkeys(STATES, 0.0)
        i = max(0, bisect.bisect_right(self.span_starts, since) - 1)
        while i < len(self.spans) and self.spans[i][0] < until:
            a, b, state = self.spans[i]
            lo, hi = max(a, since), min(b, until)
            if hi > lo:
                totals[state] += (hi - lo).total_seconds() / 60
            i += 1
        covered = (min(until, self.now) - since).total_seconds() / 60
        totals[NO_TICKS] += max(0.0, covered - sum(totals.values()))
        return {k: round(v, 1) for k, v in totals.items()}

    def figures(self, since, until):
        """Every figure for [since, until)."""
        hours = (until - since).total_seconds() / 3600
        lo = bisect.bisect_left(self.merge_times, since)
        hi = bisect.bisect_left(self.merge_times, until)
        merges = self.merges[lo:hi]
        n = len(merges)
        runs = self.runs[bisect.bisect_left(self.run_times, since):
                         bisect.bisect_left(self.run_times, until)]
        ticks = self.records[bisect.bisect_left(self.tick_times, since):
                             bisect.bisect_left(self.tick_times, until)]
        out = {"since": stamp(since), "until": stamp(until),
               "hours": round(hours, 2), "merges": n,
               "merges_per_hour": ratio(n, hours, 1),
               "states": self.state_minutes(since, until)}
        out["arrivals"] = sum(1 for t in self.arrived.values()
                              if since <= t < until)
        out["arrivals_per_hour"] = ratio(out["arrivals"], hours, 1)
        # designs/0047: approvals an hour, the supply of work, by the
        # first tick that listed each pull request.
        out["approvals"] = sum(1 for t in self.first_approved.values()
                               if since <= t < until)
        out["approvals_per_hour"] = ratio(out["approvals"], hours, 1)
        out["runs_per_hour"] = ratio(len(runs), hours, 1)
        out["eligible_mean"] = ratio(sum(len(r.get("queue") or [])
                                         for r in ticks), len(ticks), 1)
        out["held_mean"] = ratio(sum(len(r.get("held") or {})
                                     for r in ticks), len(ticks), 1)
        out.update(self._efficiency(merges, runs, since, until))
        out.update(self._rework(merges, runs, since, until))
        out["approval_to_merge"] = self._latency(merges)
        out.update(self._capacity(runs, hours))
        out["busy"] = self._busy(since, until)
        out.update(self._policy(ticks, hours))
        out["hand_backs_per_hour"] = ratio(out["hand_backs"]["told"], hours,
                                           1)
        return out

    def _efficiency(self, merges, runs, since, until):
        per_pr, heads, batches = [], [], []
        for m in merges:
            h = bisect.bisect_right(self.head_runs.get(m["pr"], []), m["t"])
            b = bisect.bisect_right(self.batch_runs.get(m["pr"], []),
                                    m["t"])
            per_pr.append(h + b)
            heads.append(h)
            batches.append(b)
        n = len(merges)
        kinds = collections.Counter(r["kind"] for r in runs)
        slots = collections.Counter(m["basis"] for m in merges)
        sizes = list(slots.values())
        tops = {"green": 0, "all": 0, "part": 0, "none": 0}
        members_total = 0
        for run in runs:
            if run["kind"] != "ahead" or not run["end"] or \
                    run["end"]["res"] != "green":
                continue
            got = set(self.merged_on.get(("ahead", run["pr"],
                                          run["sha"][:10]), ()))
            members = run["members"]
            tops["green"] += 1
            members_total += len(members)
            on = len(got & set(members))
            tops["all" if on == len(members) else "part" if on
                 else "none"] += 1
        return {
            "runs_per_merged_pr": dict(spread(per_pr), mean=ratio(
                sum(per_pr), n), heads_mean=ratio(sum(heads), n),
                batches_mean=ratio(sum(batches), n)),
            "runs": dict(kinds), "runs_total": len(runs),
            "runs_per_merge": ratio(len(runs), n),
            "merge_slots": {
                "slots": len(sizes), "prs_per_slot": ratio(n, len(sizes)),
                "sizes": {"1": sum(1 for s in sizes if s == 1),
                          "2-3": sum(1 for s in sizes if 2 <= s <= 3),
                          "4+": sum(1 for s in sizes if s >= 4)},
                "unknown": sum(1 for b in slots if b[0] == "unknown")},
            "green_batch_tops": tops,
            # designs/0047: pull requests per green batch top or train.
            "prs_per_green_top": ratio(members_total, tops["green"])}

    def _rework(self, merges, runs, since, until):
        n = len(merges)
        told = [h for h in self.hand_backs if since <= h["t"] < until]
        first = collections.Counter(h["cause"] for h in told
                                    if not h["repeat"])
        again = collections.Counter(h["cause"] for h in told if h["repeat"])
        reds, tops = collections.Counter(), collections.Counter()
        for run in runs:
            end = run["end"]
            if not end or end["res"] not in ("green", "red"):
                continue
            if run["kind"] in ("head", LANE):
                reds["green" if end["res"] == "green" else
                     "red(merge)" if end["steps"] == "merge" else "red"] += 1
            elif run["kind"] == "ahead":
                tops[end["res"]] += 1
        return {"hand_backs": {
            "told": len(told), "per_merge": ratio(len(told), n),
            "new": dict(first), "repeats": dict(again),
            "repeats_total": sum(again.values()),
            "per_merge_by_cause": {c: ratio(v, n) for c, v in (
                first + again).most_common()}},
            "head_checks": dict(reds), "batch_checks": dict(tops)}

    def _latency(self, merges):
        local, remote = [], []
        for m in merges:
            seen = self.first_approved.get(m["pr"])
            if seen is not None:
                local.append((m["t"] - seen).total_seconds() / 60)
            got = self.approvals.get(str(m["pr"]))
            if got:
                remote.append((m["t"] - parse_time(got)).total_seconds()
                              / 60)
        out = {"local_minutes": {k: (round(v) if isinstance(v, float)
                                     else v)
                                 for k, v in spread(local).items()}}
        if self.approvals:
            out["github_minutes"] = {k: (round(v) if isinstance(v, float)
                                         else v)
                                     for k, v in spread(remote).items()}
        return out

    def _capacity(self, runs, hours):
        by = collections.Counter()
        for run in runs:
            by[category(run)] += run["dur"] / 3600
        waited = [r["end"]["waited"] for r in runs
                  if r["kind"] in ("head", LANE) and r["end"]
                  and r["end"]["waited"] is not None]
        ran = [r["end"]["ran"] for r in runs if built(r)]
        return {"slot_hours": {k: round(v, 1) for k, v in by.most_common()},
                "slot_hours_used": round(sum(by.values()), 1),
                "slot_hours_available": round(self.slots * hours, 1),
                "slots": self.slots,
                "head_wait_seconds": spread(waited),
                "run_seconds": dict(spread(ran), mean=mean(ran)),
                "run_seconds_by_kind": run_times(runs)}

    def _busy(self, since, until):
        """{name: {busy, listed hours, reviewer}}: the share of the time
        an agent was listed (not gone) that she was `busy`: `idle`,
        `shell` (her turn over, a background task running; designs/0017)
        and anything else count as not busy."""
        out = {}
        for name, spans in self.presence_spans.items():
            busy = listed = 0.0
            for a, b, status in spans:
                lo, hi = max(a, since), min(b, until)
                if hi <= lo or status == "gone":
                    continue
                seconds = (hi - lo).total_seconds()
                listed += seconds
                if status == "busy":
                    busy += seconds
            if listed:
                out[name] = {"busy": round(busy / listed, 3),
                             "listed_hours": round(listed / 3600, 1),
                             "reviewer": name in self.reviewers}
        return dict(sorted(out.items(), key=lambda kv: (
            not kv[1]["reviewer"], -kv[1]["busy"], kv[0])))

    def _policy(self, ticks, hours):
        held = sum(1 for r in ticks if r.get("right_of_way"))
        recuts = sum(1 for t in self.recut_times
                     if ticks and ticks[0]["_t"] <= t <= ticks[-1]["_t"])
        # designs/0047: what cut a started batch or a train again, by
        # the Merger's train events ("other" when it names none), and,
        # in a dry run, the trains' own changes and the batch re-cuts
        # trains would not have made.
        causes, dry = collections.Counter(), collections.Counter()
        for r in ticks:
            said = [c for c in r.get("train_events") or ()
                    if c not in ("cut", "kept")]
            if r.get("trains_dry"):
                dry.update(said)
                said = []
            if r.get("recut"):
                causes.update(said or ["other"])
        return {"recuts_by_cause": dict(causes.most_common()),
                "dry_train_changes": dict(dry.most_common()),
                "recuts_avoided": sum(1 for r in ticks
                                      if r.get("recut_avoided")),
                "right_of_way_share": ratio(held, len(ticks), 3),
                "overdue_mean": ratio(sum(len(r.get("overdue") or {})
                                          for r in ticks), len(ticks), 1),
                "recuts": recuts, "recuts_per_hour": ratio(recuts, hours, 1)}

    # ------------------------------------------------------ now

    def snapshot(self):
        """Where the pull requests wait at the last tick, and who holds
        right of way."""
        if not self.records:
            return {}
        last = self.records[-1]
        batch = list(last.get("batch") or [])
        later = [pr for part in last.get("later") or [] for pr in part]
        back = sorted({d.get("pr") for d in last.get("decisions") or []
                       if d.get("action") in ("HAND-BACK", "SKIP")})
        queued = [pr for pr in last.get("queue") or []
                  if pr not in batch and pr not in later and pr not in back]
        held = collections.defaultdict(list)
        for pr, reason in sorted((last.get("held") or {}).items(),
                                 key=lambda kv: int(kv[0])):
            held[hold_kind(reason)].append(int(pr))
        row = last.get("right_of_way") or {}
        since = None
        if row.get("pr") is not None:
            for record in reversed(self.records):
                if (record.get("right_of_way") or {}).get("pr") != row["pr"]:
                    break
                since = record["_t"]
        reasons = {}
        for pr in back:
            said = self.handed_back.get(str(pr))
            if isinstance(said, dict):
                reasons[pr] = stats.cause_of(said.get("reason") or "")
        return {"at": stamp(last["_t"]), "state": last["_state"],
                "batch": batch, "later": later, "queued": queued,
                "handed_back": back, "handed_back_causes": reasons,
                "held": dict(held),
                "right_of_way": {"pr": row.get("pr"),
                                 "since": stamp(since) if since else None},
                "overdue": len(last.get("overdue") or {}),
                "searching": last["_state"] == SEARCH}

    def stacks(self):
        """The stacks waiting at the last tick, largest first: each a
        tree from the Merger's `stacked on #N` holds, rooted at the
        pull request at the bottom (based on the default branch), with
        where that root waits now."""
        if not self.records:
            return []
        last = self.records[-1]
        held = {int(k): str(v) for k, v in (last.get("held") or {}).items()}
        below = {}
        for pr, reason in held.items():
            got = STACKED_RE.search(reason)
            if got:
                below[pr] = int(got.group(1))
        above = collections.defaultdict(list)
        for pr, base in below.items():
            above[base].append(pr)

        def tree(pr, seen):
            seen = seen | {pr}
            kids = [tree(k, seen) for k in sorted(above.get(pr, ()))
                    if k not in seen]
            return {"pr": pr, "layers": kids,
                    "count": sum(1 + k["count"] for k in kids),
                    "depth": max((1 + k["depth"] for k in kids), default=0)}
        snap = self.snapshot()
        cut = self.trains()
        trains = {pr: t["train"] for t in cut for pr in t["prs"]}

        def mark(node):
            node["status"], node["why"] = self.status(node["pr"], cut, snap)
            for k in node["layers"]:
                mark(k)
        roots = []
        for root in {pr for pr in above if pr not in below} | {
                base for base in below.values() if base not in below}:
            t = tree(root, frozenset())
            if trains.get(root) is not None:
                where = "in train %d" % trains[root]
            elif root in trains:
                where = "predicted, not yet in a train"
            elif root in held:
                where = "held: %s" % held[root]
            elif root in snap.get("handed_back", ()):
                where = "back with the author"
            elif root in (last.get("queue") or ()):
                where = "in the queue"
            else:
                where = "not a candidate (not approved, its own check " \
                        "not green, or not open)"
            t["root_where"] = where
            mark(t)
            roots.append(t)
        roots.sort(key=lambda t: (-t["count"], t["pr"]))
        return roots

    def singles(self):
        """The candidates at the last tick that are in no stack (neither
        a base nor a layer): the queue's and the held ones, in queue
        order then by number, each with its status dot."""
        if not self.records:
            return []
        last = self.records[-1]
        held = {int(k): str(v) for k, v in (last.get("held") or {}).items()}
        stacked = set()
        for pr, reason in held.items():
            got = STACKED_RE.search(reason)
            if got:
                stacked |= {pr, int(got.group(1))}
        order = []
        for pr in list(last.get("queue") or ()) + sorted(held):
            if isinstance(pr, int) and pr not in stacked and pr not in order:
                order.append(pr)
        snap, cut = self.snapshot(), self.trains()
        out = []
        for pr in order:
            status, why = self.status(pr, cut, snap)
            out.append({"pr": pr, "status": status, "why": why})
        return out

    def trains(self):
        """The trains in ahead.json now, the first being merged or
        tested: each with its carriages, its top (the commit tested for
        it), whether its top's run is waiting, testing or done, and
        whether it was cut for urgent pull requests."""
        entries = []
        for e in self.ahead.get("entries") or ():
            try:
                entries.append(dict(e, pr=int(e["pr"])))
            except (TypeError, KeyError, ValueError):
                continue
        if not entries:
            return []
        urgent = set(self.ahead.get("urgent_cut") or ())
        said = str((self.ahead.get("batch") or {}).get("said") or "")
        groups = collections.OrderedDict()
        if all("train" in e for e in entries):
            for e in entries:
                groups.setdefault(e["train"], []).append(e)
        else:
            # Without trains, the batch and the later batches, by size;
            # the rest are predicted but not yet cut into one.
            sizes = [(self.ahead.get("batch") or {}).get("size")] + [
                (part or {}).get("size")
                for part in self.ahead.get("later") or ()]
            at = 0
            for n, size in enumerate(sizes):
                if not isinstance(size, int) or size < 1:
                    break
                if entries[at:at + size]:
                    groups[n] = entries[at:at + size]
                at += size
            if entries[at:]:
                groups[None] = entries[at:]
        out = []
        below = {}
        if self.records:
            for pr, reason in (self.records[-1].get("held") or {}).items():
                got = STACKED_RE.search(str(reason))
                if got and str(pr).isdigit():
                    below[int(pr)] = int(got.group(1))
        for n, (train, cars) in enumerate(groups.items()):
            if train is None:
                out.append({"train": None, "prs": [e["pr"] for e in cars],
                            "carriages": [[e["pr"]] for e in cars],
                            "top": None, "state": "predicted, not yet in "
                            "a train", "since": None, "urgent": False})
                continue
            top = str(cars[-1].get("sha") or "")
            run = None
            for r in reversed(self.runs):
                if r["kind"] == "ahead" and top and r["sha"] and \
                        top.startswith(r["sha"][:10]):
                    run = r
                    break
            if n == 0 and "green" in said:
                state = "green, merging"
            elif run is None:
                state = "waiting for a slot"
            elif run["end"] is None:
                state = "testing"
            else:
                state = run["end"]["res"]
            out.append({
                # Counted from 1, as the Merger's log counts them
                # (TRAIN-CUT 1, 2, ...); entries count from 0.
                "train": train + 1 if isinstance(train, int) else train,
                "prs": [e["pr"] for e in cars],
                "carriages": carriages_of(cars, below),
                "top": top[:10], "state": state,
                "since": stamp(run["t"]) if run else None,
                "urgent": bool(urgent & {e["pr"] for e in cars})})
        return out

    # ------------------------------------------------- status, priority

    def own_check(self, pr):
        """What the build check last said of `pr`'s own head: "running",
        a run's result ("green", "red", "red(merge)", "stopped"), or None
        when it has run nothing for it. A green it posted without a
        run (MATCHED, COVERED) counts. The head is the last one it ran,
        which may since have been pushed over."""
        said = []
        for run in self.runs:
            if run["pr"] == pr and run["kind"] in ("head", LANE):
                said.append((run["end"]["t"], run["end"]["res"])
                            if run["end"] else (run["t"], "running"))
        for (number, _), greens in self.events.items():
            if number == pr:
                said.extend((at, "green") for at, _ in greens)
        return max(said, key=lambda s: s[0])[1] if said else None

    def _fixes(self):
        """(nightly, main_red): the open pull requests that fix a red
        nightly (forge-nightly's file, while fresh and its issue is
        open) and a red default branch (the build check's state.json,
        while its issue is open), as the Merger reads them."""
        got = load_json(os.path.join(self.state_dir, "nightly",
                                     nightly.NIGHTLY_FILE), {})
        night = set()
        try:
            fresh = self.now - nightly.parse_time(got["at"]) <= nightly.FRESH
        except (KeyError, TypeError, ValueError, AttributeError):
            fresh = False
        if fresh and got.get("issue_open") and isinstance(
                got.get("fixes"), list):
            night = {n for n in got["fixes"] if isinstance(n, int)
                     and not isinstance(n, bool)}
        red = (load_json(os.path.join(self.state_dir, "pr-check",
                                      "state.json"), {}) or {}).get(
            "main_red")
        main = set()
        if isinstance(red, dict) and red.get("issue") and isinstance(
                red.get("fixes"), list):
            main = {n for n in red["fixes"] if isinstance(n, int)
                    and not isinstance(n, bool)}
        return night, main

    def priorities(self):
        """{str(pr): {"level", "why"}} for the pull requests the Merger
        puts ahead of the rest: `urgent` for those carrying
        labels.urgent, `elevated` for the others it treats as urgent
        (a red nightly's or default branch's fix) and for the one with
        right of way. Normal ones are left out.

        The labels come from GitHub with --github; otherwise from the
        Merger's last record (`urgent`, `elevated`) when it has them;
        otherwise they are inferred: ahead.json's `urgent_cut` lists every queued pull
        request the Merger found urgent, so one there that fixes
        nothing red carries the label."""
        night, main = self._fixes()
        labelled = self.labelled
        last = self.records[-1] if self.records else {}
        if labelled is None and isinstance(last.get("urgent"), list):
            # forge-merger records each tick's labelled and elevated pull
            # requests, held ones and layers too: its view is the one.
            labelled = {n for n in last["urgent"] if isinstance(n, int)}
        raised = ({n for n in last["elevated"] if isinstance(n, int)}
                  if isinstance(last.get("elevated"), list) else set())
        inferred = labelled is None
        if inferred:
            labelled = {n for n in self.ahead.get("urgent_cut") or ()
                        if isinstance(n, int)} - night - main
        out = {}

        def put(pr, level, why):
            out.setdefault(str(pr), {"level": level, "why": why})
        for pr in sorted(labelled):
            put(pr, URGENT, "urgent: carries the urgent label%s" % (
                " (the Merger cut a train for it and it fixes nothing "
                "red)" if inferred else ""))
        for pr in sorted(main):
            put(pr, ELEVATED, "elevated: fixes the red default branch")
        for pr in sorted(night):
            put(pr, ELEVATED, "elevated: fixes the red nightly")
        for pr in sorted(raised - main - night):
            put(pr, ELEVATED, "elevated: the Merger treats it as urgent")
        row = ((self.records[-1].get("right_of_way") or {})
               if self.records else {}).get("pr")
        if isinstance(row, int):
            put(row, ELEVATED, "elevated: has right of way")
        return out

    def handed_back_at(self, pr):
        """(when, why) of the Merger's hand-back of `pr` at the head
        its last decision names, or None: a hand-back at an earlier
        tick, which a later record's queue doesn't undo, holds until a
        new head (2026-11-12: #10608, handed back at 16:06, showed green
        an hour later)."""
        if self._backs is None:
            backs, heads = {}, {}
            for r in self.records:
                for d in r.get("decisions") or ():
                    n, head = d.get("pr"), d.get("head")
                    if not isinstance(n, int) or not head:
                        continue
                    heads[n] = head
                    if d.get("action") == "HAND-BACK" and d.get(
                            "result") in ("done", "already said"):
                        backs[n] = (head, stamp(r["_t"]),
                                    str(d.get("reason") or "no reason "
                                        "given"))
            self._backs = {n: b[1:] for n, b in backs.items()
                           if heads.get(n) == b[0]}
        return self._backs.get(pr)

    def status(self, pr, trains=None, snap=None):
        """(colour, why) for `pr` at the last tick, for a stack's status
        dot: green, it can merge (eligible, or a layer whose own check
        is green, waiting only for the one below; or a member of a
        green train); orange, testing is underway (its own check, or
        the train it is in, is running or waiting for a slot, or its
        hold waits on a check); red, it cannot merge as it is (any
        other hold, handed back, red, or not a candidate). The
        Merger's last record decides first, then the build check."""
        if not self.records:
            return RED, "no Merger record"
        last = self.records[-1]
        trains = self.trains() if trains is None else trains
        snap = self.snapshot() if snap is None else snap
        held = {int(k): str(v) for k, v in (last.get("held") or {}).items()}
        queue = set(last.get("queue") or ())
        for t in trains:
            if pr not in t["prs"] or t["train"] is None:
                continue
            state = t["state"]
            if state.startswith("green"):
                return GREEN, "in train %d, green: merging" % t["train"]
            if state == "red":
                return RED, "in train %d, whose top is red" % t["train"]
            return ORANGE, "in train %d: %s" % (t["train"], state)
        if pr in snap.get("handed_back", ()):
            return RED, "handed back to its author"
        back = self.handed_back_at(pr)
        if back:
            return RED, "handed back at %s: %s" % back
        gone = {int(g.group(1)) for g in (MERGED_BELOW_RE.search(r)
                                          for r in held.values()) if g}
        if pr not in held and pr not in queue and (pr in gone or any(
                m["pr"] == pr for m in self.merges)):
            return GREEN, "merged"
        own = self.own_check(pr)
        if pr in held:
            reason = held[pr]
            got = STACKED_ONLY_RE.match(reason)
            if got:
                below = "waits for #%s below it" % got.group(1)
                if own == "green":
                    return GREEN, "approved, its own check green; %s" % below
                if own in (None, "running", "stopped"):
                    return ORANGE, "approved, its own check %s; %s" % (
                        "not run yet" if own is None else own, below)
                return RED, "its own check is %s; %s" % (own, below)
            if any(w in reason for w in UNDERWAY):
                return ORANGE, "held: %s" % reason
            return RED, "held: %s" % reason
        if pr in queue:
            if own == "running":
                return ORANGE, "eligible, its own check running"
            return GREEN, "eligible: in the Merger's queue"
        return RED, ("not a candidate (not approved, its own check not "
                     "green, or not open)")

    # ------------------------------------------------- recent trains

    def recent_trains(self, limit=RECENT_TRAINS):
        """The last `limit` trains the Merger cut, newest first, and
        what became of each and of each member, from merger.jsonl alone
        (and the build check's runs of their tops).

        A record's `trains` (live, not `trains_dry`) lists each train's
        pull requests. A train there that is a subset of what is left of
        one before goes on as that train; any other was cut that tick,
        and so was every train when `train_events` says the default
        branch moved. A member leaves its train by a MERGE (`train`:
        true is the train's own merge), a hand-back (`suspect`: true is
        the culprit a red train's search found red on its own), by
        boarding a train cut later (re-cut), or by going missing from
        the trains (left: its hold says why, else a push, a lost
        approval or a close). A record without `trains` (a search going
        on, say) only settles members by its decisions."""
        cut, active = [], []
        # A record's `trains` are as cut before its own merges: a member
        # merged is never a train again (#10777 on 2026-11-12 showed as
        # cut a second time, the tick it merged).
        merged = set()

        def settle(t, pr, outcome, why, at):
            if pr in t["current"]:
                t["current"].remove(pr)
            t["out"][str(pr)] = {"outcome": outcome, "why": why,
                                 "at": stamp(at)}
            t["last"] = at

        for r in self.records:
            at = r["_t"]
            held = {str(k): str(v) for k, v in (r.get("held") or {}).items()}
            for d in r.get("decisions") or ():
                pr = d.get("pr")
                if d.get("action") == "MERGE" \
                        and d.get("result", "done") == "done":
                    merged.add(pr)
                owner = next((t for t in active if pr in t["current"]), None)
                if owner is None:
                    continue
                action = d.get("action")
                if action == "MERGE" and d.get("result", "done") == "done":
                    settle(owner, pr, "merged", "merged in the train's own "
                           "merge" if d.get("train") else "merged on its own",
                           at)
                elif action == "HAND-BACK" and d.get("suspect"):
                    settle(owner, pr, "culprit", "red on its own, found by "
                           "the red train's search; handed back", at)
                elif action == "HAND-BACK" and d.get("result") in (
                        "done", "already said"):
                    settle(owner, pr, "left", "handed back: %s" % (
                        d.get("reason") or "no reason given"), at)
            for t in [t for t in active if not t["current"]]:
                active.remove(t)
                t["end"] = t["last"]
            if r.get("trains_dry") or "trains" not in r:
                continue
            events = [str(e) for e in r.get("train_events") or ()]
            lists = [[n for n in part if isinstance(n, int)
                      and n not in merged]
                     for part in r.get("trains") or () if part]
            lists = [part for part in lists if part]
            fresh, going = [], {}
            for part in lists:
                t = None
                if "main moved" not in events:
                    t = next((a for a in active if id(a) not in going
                              and set(part) <= set(a["current"])), None)
                if t is None:
                    below = {}
                    for pr, reason in held.items():
                        got = STACKED_RE.search(reason)
                        if got and pr.isdigit():
                            below[int(pr)] = int(got.group(1))
                    t = {"cut_t": at, "prs": list(part),
                         "carriages": carriages_of(
                             [{"pr": n} for n in part], below),
                         "current": list(part), "out": {}, "end": None,
                         "last": at, "events": events}
                    fresh.append(t)
                going[id(t)] = part
            on_new = {pr: t for t in fresh for pr in t["prs"]}
            why_recut = "; ".join(RECUT_SAYS.get(e, e) for e in events
                                  if e not in ("cut", "kept")) or \
                "cut again"
            for t in list(active):
                keep = going.get(id(t), ())
                for pr in [p for p in t["current"] if p not in keep]:
                    if pr in on_new:
                        settle(t, pr, "recut", "re-cut into the train cut "
                               "at %s (%s)" % (stamp(at), why_recut), at)
                    else:
                        settle(t, pr, "left", "left the trains: %s" % (
                            held.get(str(pr)) or "a push, a lost approval "
                            "or a close took it out of the queue"), at)
                if not t["current"]:
                    active.remove(t)
                    t["end"] = at
                    t["ended_by"] = why_recut
            active.extend(fresh)
            cut.extend(fresh)
        out = []
        for t in cut[-limit:][::-1] if limit > 0 else ():
            out.append(self._train_story(t))
        return out

    def _train_story(self, t):
        """One train of `recent_trains`, as the page shows it."""
        end = t["end"]
        until = end or self.now
        runs = [r for r in self.runs if r["kind"] == "ahead"
                and r["pr"] in t["prs"] and t["cut_t"] <= r["t"] <= until]
        tops = [{"pr": r["pr"], "sha": r["sha"][:10],
                 "res": r["end"]["res"] if r["end"] else "running",
                 "ran": r["end"]["ran"] if r["end"] else None,
                 "at": stamp(r["t"])} for r in runs]
        red = any(x["res"].startswith("red") for x in tops)
        searched = any(r.get("_state") == SEARCH for r in self.records
                       if t["cut_t"] <= r["_t"] <= until)
        members = {}
        for pr in t["prs"]:
            members[str(pr)] = t["out"].get(str(pr)) or {
                "outcome": "waiting", "why": "still in this train",
                "at": None}
        kinds = collections.Counter(m["outcome"] for m in members.values())
        merged = kinds["merged"]
        culprits = sorted(int(k) for k, m in members.items()
                          if m["outcome"] == "culprit")
        if end is None:
            outcome = "running"
            why = "still on its way"
        elif merged == len(t["prs"]):
            outcome = "merged"
            why = "all %d merged%s" % (merged, " in one train merge" if all(
                "own merge" in m["why"] for m in members.values()) else "")
        elif merged:
            outcome = "partly merged"
            why = "%d of %d merged" % (merged, len(t["prs"]))
        elif red or culprits:
            outcome = "red"
            why = "its top went red"
        else:
            outcome = "re-cut"
            why = "every member left" if kinds["left"] == len(
                t["prs"]) else t.get("ended_by") or "cut again"
        if outcome != "running" and (red or culprits):
            why += "; red%s%s" % (
                ", searched" if searched else "",
                "; culprit %s" % ", ".join("#%d" % n for n in culprits)
                if culprits else "")
        if outcome in ("merged", "partly merged", "running") and \
                kinds["recut"]:
            why += "; %d re-cut into a later train" % kinds["recut"]
        if kinds["left"] and outcome != "re-cut":
            why += "; %d left" % kinds["left"]
        return {"cut": stamp(t["cut_t"]), "end": stamp(end) if end else None,
                "minutes": int((until - t["cut_t"]).total_seconds() // 60),
                "prs": t["prs"], "carriages": t["carriages"],
                "outcome": outcome, "why": why, "members": members,
                "tops": tops, "searched": searched}

    def hourly(self, hours=24):
        """The last `hours` clock hours, oldest first: each hour's
        states, merges and arrivals."""
        top = self.now.replace(minute=0, second=0, microsecond=0)
        rows = []
        for k in range(hours - 1, -1, -1):
            a = top - k * HOUR
            b = min(a + HOUR, self.now)
            lo = bisect.bisect_left(self.merge_times, a)
            rows.append({"hour": stamp(a), "states": self.state_minutes(a, b),
                         "merges": bisect.bisect_left(self.merge_times, b)
                         - lo,
                         "arrivals": sum(1 for t in self.arrived.values()
                                         if a <= t < b)})
        return rows

    def graph_hours(self, hours=24):
        """The last `hours` whole clock hours, oldest first, with what
        the page graphs (graph_row), then the hour under way, to now,
        with `partial` and its `until`. An hour with no Merger record
        is a gap: it has only its `hour`, and `records` false."""
        top = self.now.replace(minute=0, second=0, microsecond=0)
        rows = []
        for k in range(hours, -1, -1):
            a = top - k * HOUR
            b = min(a + HOUR, self.now)
            if b <= a:
                continue
            ticks = (bisect.bisect_left(self.tick_times, b)
                     - bisect.bisect_left(self.tick_times, a))
            row = {"hour": stamp(a), "records": bool(ticks)}
            if k == 0:
                row.update(partial=True, until=stamp(b))
            if ticks:
                row.update(graph_row(self.figures(a, b)))
            rows.append(row)
        return rows

    def build_times(self, days=HISTORY_DAYS, size=BUCKET_HOURS):
        """The build check's run times over the last `days`, in buckets
        of `size` hours from midnight UTC, oldest first: each bucket's
        run_times(). The last bucket runs to now and is `partial`."""
        step = size * HOUR
        top = self.now.replace(hour=self.now.hour - self.now.hour % size,
                               minute=0, second=0, microsecond=0)
        rows = []
        for k in range(days * 24 // size - 1, -1, -1):
            a = top - k * step
            b = min(a + step, self.now)
            runs = self.runs[bisect.bisect_left(self.run_times, a):
                             bisect.bisect_left(self.run_times, b)]
            rows.append(dict({"since": stamp(a), "until": stamp(b),
                              "partial": b < a + step}, **run_times(runs)))
        return rows

    def watch_figures(self, since, until):
        """forge-stats-watch's figures (designs/0045): {name: (value,
        samples)}."""
        got = self.figures(since, until)
        hours = (until - since).total_seconds() / 3600
        busy = [v["busy"] for v in got["busy"].values()
                if v["reviewer"] and v["listed_hours"] >= 0.9 * hours]
        slots = got["merge_slots"]
        return {"hand_backs_per_merge": (got["hand_backs"]["per_merge"],
                                         got["merges"]),
                "prs_per_slot": (slots["prs_per_slot"], slots["slots"]),
                "reviewer_busy": (100 * max(busy) if busy else None,
                                  len(busy))}


# ------------------------------------------------------------- history

HISTORY_KEYS = ("merges", "arrivals", "states", "runs_total",
                "runs_per_merge", "merge_slots", "hand_backs",
                "head_checks", "batch_checks", "slot_hours", "recuts",
                "right_of_way_share",
                "overdue_mean", "runs_per_merged_pr", "approval_to_merge",
                "run_seconds", "run_seconds_by_kind")


def graph_row(fig):
    """What the page graphs of one hour, from its figures or its
    history line (whose older lines lack some: those are None)."""
    lat = fig.get("approval_to_merge") or {}
    lat = lat.get("github_minutes") or lat.get("local_minutes") or {}
    return {"merges": fig.get("merges"),
            "runs_per_merge": fig.get("runs_per_merge"),
            "runs_per_merged_pr": (fig.get("runs_per_merged_pr")
                                   or {}).get("mean"),
            "prs_per_slot": (fig.get("merge_slots")
                             or {}).get("prs_per_slot"),
            "approval_median": lat.get("median"),
            "approval_p90": lat.get("p90"),
            "approval_n": lat.get("n")}


def had_records(line):
    """Whether a history line's hour had the Merger ticking at all."""
    states = line.get("states") or {}
    return any(v for k, v in states.items() if k != NO_TICKS)


def history_lines(lines):
    """{hour: line} of flow-history.jsonl's lines."""
    out = {}
    for line in lines:
        try:
            got = json.loads(line)
            states = got.get("states")
            if isinstance(states, dict):
                for old, new in LEGACY_STATES.items():
                    if old in states:
                        states[new] = states.get(new, 0) + states.pop(old)
            out[got["hour"]] = got
        except (ValueError, KeyError, TypeError):
            continue
    return out


def graph_hours_from_history(history, until, hours=24):
    """Flow.graph_hours() from flow-history.jsonl's lines, for a saved
    flow.json written before the page had graphs. An hour with no line,
    or no Merger record, is a gap."""
    by = history_lines(history)
    top = until.replace(minute=0, second=0, microsecond=0)
    rows = []
    for k in range(hours, 0, -1):
        hour = stamp(top - k * HOUR)
        line = by.get(hour)
        row = {"hour": hour, "records": bool(line and had_records(line))}
        if row["records"]:
            row.update(graph_row(line))
        rows.append(row)
    return rows


def build_times_from_history(history, until, days=HISTORY_DAYS,
                             size=BUCKET_HOURS):
    """Flow.build_times() from flow-history.jsonl's lines: each
    bucket's mean is its hours' means weighted by their runs. A median
    can't be put together from hours', so it is None."""
    by = history_lines(history)
    step = size * HOUR
    top = until.replace(hour=until.hour - until.hour % size, minute=0,
                        second=0, microsecond=0)
    rows = []
    for k in range(days * 24 // size - 1, -1, -1):
        a = top - k * step
        b = min(a + step, until)
        row = {"since": stamp(a), "until": stamp(b),
               "partial": b < a + step}
        for name, _ in RUN_KINDS:
            n = total = 0
            for h in range(size):
                got = ((by.get(stamp(a + h * HOUR)) or {})
                       .get("run_seconds_by_kind") or {}).get(name) or {}
                if got.get("n") and got.get("mean") is not None:
                    n += got["n"]
                    total += got["n"] * got["mean"]
            row[name] = {"n": n, "mean": round(total / n) if n else None,
                         "median": None, "p90": None}
        rows.append(row)
    return rows


def with_graphs(data, history):
    """`data` (a flow.json), with the graphs' figures from
    flow-history.jsonl's lines where it has none of its own."""
    data = dict(data)
    until = parse_time(data["generated"])
    if "graph_hours" not in data:
        data["graph_hours"] = graph_hours_from_history(history, until)
    if "build_times" not in data:
        data["build_times"] = build_times_from_history(history, until)
    return data


def append_history(flow, path):
    """Append one line for each whole hour not yet in `path`, from at
    most HISTORY_DAYS ago. Returns how many were added."""
    last = None
    for line in read_lines(path):
        try:
            last = parse_time(json.loads(line)["hour"])
        except (ValueError, KeyError, TypeError, AttributeError):
            continue
    top = flow.now.replace(minute=0, second=0, microsecond=0)
    first = top - HISTORY_DAYS * DAY
    if flow.records:
        # The first whole hour the records cover.
        start = flow.records[0]["_t"]
        hour = start.replace(minute=0, second=0, microsecond=0)
        first = max(first, hour if hour == start else hour + HOUR)
    if last is not None:
        first = max(first, last + HOUR)
    lines = []
    hour = first
    while hour + HOUR <= top:
        got = flow.figures(hour, hour + HOUR)
        lines.append(json.dumps(dict({"hour": stamp(hour)}, **{
            k: got[k] for k in HISTORY_KEYS}), sort_keys=True))
        hour += HOUR
    if lines:
        with open(path, "a") as handle:
            handle.write("\n".join(lines) + "\n")
    return len(lines)


# -------------------------------------------------------------- GitHub

APPROVAL_FIELDS = ("number reviews(states: APPROVED, first: 1) "
                   "{ nodes { submittedAt } }")


def first_approvals(token, repo, numbers, cache, call=github.api_call):
    """`cache` ({str(number): time or None}) with the first approving
    review of each of `numbers` not in it yet, from GitHub."""
    owner, name = repo.split("/", 1)
    wanted = sorted({n for n in numbers if str(n) not in cache})
    for start in range(0, len(wanted), stats.BATCH):
        part = wanted[start:start + stats.BATCH]
        body = " ".join("p%d: pullRequest(number: %d) { %s }"
                        % (n, n, APPROVAL_FIELDS) for n in part)
        status, got = github.graphql(token, stats.QUERY % body,
                                     {"owner": owner, "name": name},
                                     call=call)
        found = ((got or {}).get("data") or {}).get("repository") or {}
        if status != 200 or not found:
            raise RuntimeError("GitHub answered %s: %s"
                               % (status, json.dumps(got)[:200]))
        for n in part:
            nodes = (((found.get("p%d" % n) or {}).get("reviews") or {})
                     .get("nodes") or [])
            cache[str(n)] = nodes[0].get("submittedAt") if nodes else None
    return cache


def labelled_open(token, repo, label, call=github.api_call):
    """The open pull requests carrying `label`, a set of numbers, from
    GitHub's issue list (one request a hundred)."""
    status, items = github.paged(
        token, "/repos/%s/issues?state=open&labels=%s"
        % (repo, urllib.parse.quote(label, safe="")), call=call)
    if status != 200:
        raise RuntimeError("GitHub answered %s for the %s label"
                           % (status, label))
    return {i["number"] for i in items if isinstance(i, dict)
            and "pull_request" in i and isinstance(i.get("number"), int)}


